  "text": "{\"claims\": [{\"id\": \"C1\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"channelPool has a conns channel field of type chan *idleConn.\", \"line\": 42, \"fragment\": \"conns                    chan *idleConn\"}, {\"id\": \"C2\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"channelPool tracks an openingConns counter of type int.\", \"line\": 48, \"fragment\": \"openingConns             int\"}, {\"id\": \"C3\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"channelPool has a maxActive int field.\", \"line\": 47, \"fragment\": \"maxActive                int\"}, {\"id\": \"C4\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"channelPool has a connReqs wait queue of type []chan connReq.\", \"line\": 49, \"fragment\": \"connReqs                 []chan connReq\"}, {\"id\": \"C5\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"NewChannelPool creates conns as a buffered channel of size poolConfig.MaxIdle.\", \"line\": 70, \"fragment\": \"conns:        make(chan *idleConn, poolConfig.MaxIdle),\"}, {\"id\": \"C6\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"NewChannelPool initializes openingConns to poolConfig.InitialCap.\", \"line\": 75, \"fragment\": \"openingConns: poolConfig.InitialCap,\"}, {\"id\": \"C7\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"NewChannelPool sets c.ping only if poolConfig.Ping is non-nil.\", \"line\": 78, \"fragment\": \"if poolConfig.Ping != nil {\"}, {\"id\": \"C8\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"NewChannelPool rejects config unless InitialCap <= MaxIdle, MaxCap >= MaxIdle, and InitialCap >= 0.\", \"line\": 59, \"fragment\": \"if !(poolConfig.InitialCap <= poolConfig.MaxIdle && poolConfig.MaxCap >= poolConfig.MaxIdle && poolConfig.InitialCap >= 0) {\"}, {\"id\": \"C9\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"NewChannelPool returns an error if poolConfig.Factory is nil.\", \"line\": 62, \"fragment\": \"if poolConfig.Factory == nil {\"}, {\"id\": \"C10\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"NewChannelPool returns an error if poolConfig.Close is nil.\", \"line\": 65, \"fragment\": \"if poolConfig.Close == nil {\"}, {\"id\": \"C11\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"During initialization, if factory returns an error NewChannelPool calls c.Release() and returns a wrapped error.\", \"line\": 85, \"fragment\": \"c.Release()\"}, {\"id\": \"C12\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"During initialization each successfully factory-created connection is sent as an idleConn with timestamp time.Now() onto c.conns.\", \"line\": 88, \"fragment\": \"c.conns <- &idleConn{conn: conn, t: time.Now()}\"}, {\"id\": \"C13\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"getConns acquires c.mu.Lock, reads c.conns, then unlocks and returns it.\", \"line\": 97, \"fragment\": \"conns := c.conns\"}, {\"id\": \"C14\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"Get calls getConns to obtain the conns channel and returns ErrClosed if it is nil.\", \"line\": 105, \"fragment\": \"if conns == nil {\"}, {\"id\": \"C15\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"Get loops with a select that first tries to receive from conns.\", \"line\": 110, \"fragment\": \"case wrapConn := <-conns:\"}, {\"id\": \"C16\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"If a received wrapConn is nil, Get returns ErrClosed.\", \"line\": 111, \"fragment\": \"if wrapConn == nil {\"}, {\"id\": \"C17\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"If idleTimeout > 0 and wrapConn.t.Add(timeout) is before now, Get calls c.Close(wrapConn.conn) and continues the loop.\", \"line\": 116, \"fragment\": \"if wrapConn.t.Add(timeout).Before(time.Now()) {\"}, {\"id\": \"C18\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"If c.ping is non-nil and c.Ping(wrapConn.conn) returns an error, Get calls c.Close(wrapConn.conn) and continues the loop.\", \"line\": 124, \"fragment\": \"if err := c.Ping(wrapConn.conn); err != nil {\"}, {\"id\": \"C19\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"Get returns the received conn successfully when it passes idle-timeout and ping checks.\", \"line\": 129, \"fragment\": \"return wrapConn.conn, nil\"}, {\"id\": \"C20\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"Get's default branch acquires c.mu.Lock.\", \"line\": 131, \"fragment\": \"c.mu.Lock()\"}, {\"id\": \"C21\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"In the default branch, if openingConns >= maxActive, Get creates a connReq channel of capacity 1, appends it to connReqs, unlocks, and blocks receiving from it.\", \"line\": 134, \"fragment\": \"req := make(chan connReq, 1)\"}, {\"id\": \"C22\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"In the default branch, Get appends the new request channel to c.connReqs.\", \"line\": 135, \"fragment\": \"c.connReqs = append(c.connReqs, req)\"}, {\"id\": \"C23\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"After blocking on req, if the receive reports not ok, Get returns ErrMaxActiveConnReached.\", \"line\": 139, \"fragment\": \"return nil, ErrMaxActiveConnReached\"}, {\"id\": \"C24\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"After receiving from req, if idleTimeout > 0 and the returned idleConn timestamp is expired, Get calls c.Close and continues the loop.\", \"line\": 142, \"fragment\": \"if ret.idleConn.t.Add(timeout).Before(time.Now()) {\"}, {\"id\": \"C25\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"After a successful req receive and passing timeout check, Get returns ret.idleConn.conn.\", \"line\": 148, \"fragment\": \"return ret.idleConn.conn, nil\"}, {\"id\": \"C26\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"If c.factory is nil in the default branch, Get unlocks and returns ErrClosed.\", \"line\": 152, \"fragment\": \"return nil, ErrClosed\"}, {\"id\": \"C27\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"If c.factory() returns an error in the default branch, Get unlocks and returns that error.\", \"line\": 157, \"fragment\": \"return nil, err\"}, {\"id\": \"C28\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"After a successful factory call in the default branch, openingConns is incremented while holding c.mu, then c.mu is unlocked and the new conn returned.\", \"line\": 159, \"fragment\": \"c.openingConns++\"}, {\"id\": \"C29\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"Put returns an error if conn is nil.\", \"line\": 169, \"fragment\": \"return errors.New(\\\"connection is nil. rejecting\\\")\"}, {\"id\": \"C30\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"Put acquires c.mu.Lock before inspecting or modifying pool state.\", \"line\": 172, \"fragment\": \"c.mu.Lock()\"}, {\"id\": \"C31\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"If c.conns is nil in Put, Put unlocks and returns c.Close(conn).\", \"line\": 174, \"fragment\": \"if c.conns == nil {\"}, {\"id\": \"C32\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"If connReqs is non-empty, Put takes the first request, shifts the slice with copy, truncates it, sends a connReq with the conn, unlocks, and returns nil.\", \"line\": 179, \"fragment\": \"if l := len(c.connReqs); l > 0 {\"}, {\"id\": \"C33\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"Put performs copy(c.connReqs, c.connReqs[1:]) and reslices to l-1 when handing off to a waiter.\", \"line\": 181, \"fragment\": \"copy(c.connReqs, c.connReqs[1:])\"}, {\"id\": \"C34\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"When handing off to a waiter, Put sends a connReq containing an idleConn with timestamp time.Now() onto the request channel.\", \"line\": 183, \"fragment\": \"req <- connReq{\"}, {\"id\": \"C35\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"If connReqs is empty, Put does a non-blocking send to c.conns; on success it unlocks and returns nil.\", \"line\": 190, \"fragment\": \"case c.conns <- &idleConn{conn: conn, t: time.Now()}:\"}, {\"id\": \"C36\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"If the non-blocking send to c.conns would block, Put unlocks and calls c.Close(conn).\", \"line\": 196, \"fragment\": \"return c.Close(conn)\"}, {\"id\": \"C37\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"Close returns an error if conn is nil.\", \"line\": 204, \"fragment\": \"return errors.New(\\\"connection is nil. rejecting\\\")\"}, {\"id\": \"C38\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"Close acquires c.mu.Lock and defers c.mu.Unlock.\", \"line\": 206, \"fragment\": \"c.mu.Lock()\"}, {\"id\": \"C39\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"If c.close is nil, Close returns nil without decrementing openingConns.\", \"line\": 209, \"fragment\": \"return nil\"}, {\"id\": \"C40\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"Close decrements openingConns before invoking c.close.\", \"line\": 211, \"fragment\": \"c.openingConns--\"}, {\"id\": \"C41\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"Close invokes the close callback and returns its result.\", \"line\": 212, \"fragment\": \"return c.close(conn)\"}, {\"id\": \"C42\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"Ping returns an error if conn is nil.\", \"line\": 218, \"fragment\": \"return errors.New(\\\"connection is nil. rejecting\\\")\"}, {\"id\": \"C43\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"Ping invokes c.ping(conn) and returns its result.\", \"line\": 220, \"fragment\": \"return c.ping(conn)\"}, {\"id\": \"C44\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"Release acquires c.mu.Lock and reads c.conns into a local variable.\", \"line\": 226, \"fragment\": \"conns := c.conns\"}, {\"id\": \"C45\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"Release sets c.conns to nil.\", \"line\": 227, \"fragment\": \"c.conns = nil\"}, {\"id\": \"C46\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"Release sets c.factory to nil.\", \"line\": 228, \"fragment\": \"c.factory = nil\"}, {\"id\": \"C47\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"Release sets c.ping to nil.\", \"line\": 229, \"fragment\": \"c.ping = nil\"}, {\"id\": \"C48\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"Release saves c.close into closeFun and then sets c.close to nil.\", \"line\": 231, \"fragment\": \"c.close = nil\"}, {\"id\": \"C49\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"Release unlocks c.mu after clearing fields.\", \"line\": 232, \"fragment\": \"c.mu.Unlock()\"}, {\"id\": \"C50\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"Release returns early without closing anything if the saved conns is nil.\", \"line\": 235, \"fragment\": \"return\"}, {\"id\": \"C51\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"Release closes the saved conns channel.\", \"line\": 238, \"fragment\": \"close(conns)\"}, {\"id\": \"C52\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"Release ranges over the saved conns channel and invokes closeFun on each connection.\", \"line\": 241, \"fragment\": \"closeFun(wrapConn.conn)\"}, {\"id\": \"C53\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"Len returns the length of the channel returned by getConns.\", \"line\": 247, \"fragment\": \"return len(c.getConns())\"}, {\"id\": \"C54\", \"kind\": \"ordering\", \"statement\": \"Release sets c.conns to nil under c.mu; a subsequent Get takes the conns == nil path after acquiring the same mutex via getConns.\", \"line\": 104, \"fragment\": \"conns := c.getConns()\"}, {\"id\": \"C55\", \"kind\": \"ordering\", \"statement\": \"A Put that observes c.conns == nil (after Release) unlocks and delegates to Close, returning the result of Close.\", \"line\": 176, \"fragment\": \"return c.Close(conn)\"}, {\"id\": \"C56\", \"kind\": \"ordering\", \"statement\": \"When Get is waiting on req and Put finds a non-empty connReqs, Put sends the conn on req, which unblocks Get's receive.\", \"line\": 183, \"fragment\": \"req <- connReq{\"}, {\"id\": \"C57\", \"kind\": \"ordering\", \"statement\": \"Put removes the waiter from connReqs before sending on req, so the queue is truncated before the waiter is served.\", \"line\": 182, \"fragment\": \"c.connReqs = c.connReqs[:l-1]\"}, {\"id\": \"C58\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"Get's default branch holds c.mu while logging openingConns and maxActive.\", \"line\": 132, \"fragment\": \"log.Debugf(\\\"openConn %v %v\\\", c.openingConns, c.maxActive)\"}, {\"id\": \"C59\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"Get compares openingConns against maxActive while holding c.mu.\", \"line\": 133, \"fragment\": \"if c.openingConns >= c.maxActive {\"}, {\"id\": \"C60\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"Get unlocks c.mu after appending the request, before blocking on req.\", \"line\": 136, \"fragment\": \"c.mu.Unlock()\"}, {\"id\": \"C61\", \"kind\": \"claim\", \"statement\": \"Get unlocks c.mu before calling c.factory.\", \"line\": 154, \"fragment\": \"conn, err := c.factory()\"}, {\"id\": \"C62\", \"kind\": \"ordering\", \"statement\": \"In the default branch, Get unlocks c.mu then calls c.factory; the factory is not invoked under the mutex.\", \"line\": 154, \"fragment\": \"conn, err := c.factory()\"}], \"questions\": [\"Release closes conns and ranges over it, but connReqs waiters are neither closed nor notified by Release: what happens to a Get blocked on req when Release is called?\", \"Release sets c.conns to nil and closes the channel, but is there a guarantee that concurrent Put/Get observe consistent state given that Release unlocks before close(conns)?\", \"Get's wait-queue branch enumerates only the idle-timeout check on the handed-off idleConn (line 141-147), and the ping check is skipped; is the omission of c.ping for connReqs a requirement or an accident?\", \"Put's wait-queue handoff sends a connReq with a new idleConn timestamp even though the connection was returned later; is the timestamp reset intended?\", \"Does Close decrement openingConns even when the pool was released or the connection was never counted? No guard is present.\", \"In Get's default branch, c.factory is invoked while c.mu is unlocked; does the requirement that factory errors not alter openingConns hold for concurrent callers?\", \"Put truncates connReqs with copy and reslice but never clears the tail; does the tail retain stale channel references?\", \"Put holds c.mu across the send to a waiter channel of capacity 1; the send is non-blocking by capacity, but is the lock-held send intended?\", \"Len calls getConns which locks c.mu; is calling Len after Release required to return 0, given Release sets c.conns to nil?\", \"Release closes conns and then ranges over it; the range consumes any remaining buffered connections and calls closeFun on them. Is calling closeFun on connections still in the buffer after close(conns) intended to include everything?\", \"Release sets c.close to nil before calling closeFun; is closeFun guaranteed to be the callback captured, or could concurrent Close see nil close and skip the callback?\", \"After Release, Close returns nil when c.close is nil (line 208-209) without decrementing openingConns; is that behavior specified?\", \"Does the relation 'openingConns equals number of live connections' hold after Release, given conns channels are drained and closeFun is invoked but openingConns is not reset?\", \"Get's connReqs branch does not re-check c.conns after receiving from req; if Release occurred while Get was waiting, is Get still allowed to return ret.idleConn.conn?\", \"NewChannelPool calls c.Release() when factory errors during filling (line 85); Release closes c.conns and drains buffered connections, but does it also need to account for partially-created connections not yet enqueued?\", \"Put's non-blocking send to",
